window.docContents[164].resolve({"/Judgments-and-domains/Dynamic-judgments/#Core-C_________-natural-semantics--Judgments-and-domains--Dynamic-judgments":{"contents":"The judgment  states that the expression , under the environment  and the store , evaluates to  and yields . The store enters expressions because a function call inside an expression may change it.\n\nThe judgment  states that the expression  denotes the location .\n\nThe judgment  states that the command  yields the control , the environment  and the store . The output environment exists so that a declaration extends  for the following commands, and the block discards the extension when it ends.\n\nThe evaluator runs in the monad , which carries the derivation tree. Each rule application records its conclusion, with the rule name, at the depth of the tree. Premises are recorded before the conclusion, and bin/corecpp trace prints the tree in post order, indented by depth.\n\n","context":"Core C++, natural semantics\u0009Judgments and domains","header":"1.3. Dynamic judgments","id":"/Judgments-and-domains/Dynamic-judgments/#Core-C_________-natural-semantics--Judgments-and-domains--Dynamic-judgments"}});